#what is deployment and why use in production
In production, we use Deployments because they support rolling updates, rollbacks, self-healing, and scaling. We can release new versions gradually, strategy perform canary or blue-green deployments, and quickly roll back if an issue occurs. That's why Deployments are the standard way to manage applications in Kubernetes.genraly we in the production canary we use or we need 0 down time to we go with rollout.(rolling rollout ka mtlb ek version se dusre version me jana phir se purane version par ana ye feature hai k8s me)
**maxSurge defines the maximum number of extra Pods that can be created during a rolling update. It helps Kubernetes start new Pods before terminating old ones, ensuring high availability and zero or minimal downtime.(rolling update karte time kitna extra pod rahega taki downtime na aye.by default deplyment me rolling update strtegy hoti h or jub bhi rollout karte hai to ek revison number assign 1 hoti hai jitne bare karenge)
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment

metadata:
  name: nginx-deployment

spec:
  replicas: 5

  strategy:
    type: RollingUpdate
    rollingUpdate:
      maxSurge: 1
      maxUnavailable: 1

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx

    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:1.27
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
