#configmap 
ConfigMap — Interview Answer

ConfigMap is a Kubernetes object used to store non-sensitive configuration data separately from the application code and container image.

It allows us to pass configuration to Pods as environment variables, command-line arguments, or mounted files.

Why do we use ConfigMap?
To separate configuration from application code.
To avoid hardcoding configuration inside Docker images or Deployment YAML.
To use the same application image across Dev, Staging, and Production with different configurations.
To centrally manage application configuration.
To update configuration without rebuilding the Docker image.
#An immutable ConfigMap is a ConfigMap whose data cannot be modified after creation.

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: app-config
immutable: true

data:                           #(data me hi url or non confidential chije rakhna h.like databade url)
  APP_ENV: "production"         #key value hota hai like
  LOG_LEVEL: "info"


# ConfigMap can be used through a volume. In this case, ConfigMap data is mounted inside the container as files.
